course: dictionary
lesson: 12775
title: Edo: a name in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Edo is a name, so it starts with a capital letter. You cannot guess its meaning from ordinary words, so the clues around it matter most. «Long ago, Edo was the name of the city we now call Tokyo.» The words old name and Tokyo tell you that Edo is a place.
explain: The same name can mean different things. «The Edo period lasted from 1603 to 1868.» Here Edo means a time in history, not a city. «The Edo people live around Benin City in southern Nigeria.» Here it means a group of people. Read the words around it to find out which one is meant.
explain: Ask yourself: is it a place, a time or a people? Words like shoguns, Japan and period point to history in Japan. Words like state, Nigeria and Benin City point to Nigeria. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Edo is a name, so it begins with a capital letter.
fact: «Edo» means the old name of Tokyo in Japan, before 1868.
fact: «Edo period» means the time from 1603 to 1868 in Japanese history, when shoguns ruled from Edo.
fact: Edo is also a people and a language of southern Nigeria, around Benin City, and a state in Nigeria.
fact: Check the context: clues about Japan or shoguns mean Edo is a place or a time; clues about Nigeria mean Edo is a people, a language or a state.
exercise: «Long ago, Edo was the name of the city we now call Tokyo.» What was Edo? | *The old name of Tokyo | A river in England | A king of Japan | A city in Nigeria
exercise: «The Edo period lasted from 1603 to 1868.» What is the Edo period? | A language spoken in Benin City | A type of boat | *A time in Japanese history | A city in Nigeria
exercise: «Edo State is in southern Nigeria.» What kind of word is Edo here? | *A state in Nigeria | A period of history | A fruit from the market | The old name of a Japanese city
test: «The shoguns ruled from Edo in Japan.» Which clue tells you Edo is a place in Japan? | *The words shoguns, ruled and Japan | Edo is a short word | Edo starts with a capital letter
test: «The Edo people live around Benin City.» What are the Edo people? | A ruler of Japan | *A people of southern Nigeria | A time of 1603 to 1868 | A dish of rice
exam: Jamal reads «The Edo period was a time when shoguns ruled from Edo.» What does Edo mean in the second part? | A language of Benin City | A people of Nigeria | A state in southern Nigeria | *The city of Edo, the old name of Tokyo
